# ID: DET-03
# Name: sudo request denied
# Purpose: An account tried sudo and was refused (not in sudoers, or wrong password).
# Data: index=soc_lab sourcetype=linux_secure (Linux auth.log)
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1548.003 Sudo and Sudo Caching
# Reference implementation: detections/reference_detections.py::sudo_denied
# Expected on the synthetic datasets: svc-backup, 'user NOT in sudoers', first seen 10:08:05.
# False positives: A user who mistypes a password; an administrator missing from sudoers by mistake.
# Tuning: Alert only for accounts that should never use sudo (service accounts).
# Status: NOT TESTED in Splunk. The detection logic is tested in Python; the SPL syntax and field extractions need validation in a real Splunk.
# Lines that start with "#" are documentation. Paste only the lines below the blank line into the Splunk search bar.

index=soc_lab sourcetype=linux_secure sudo ("NOT in sudoers" OR "incorrect password attempt")
| rex "sudo:\s+(?<user>\S+)\s+:\s+(?<reason>user NOT in sudoers|\d+ incorrect password attempts?)"
| where isnotnull(reason)
| stats count earliest(_time) AS first_seen latest(_time) AS last_seen values(reason) AS reasons BY host user
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
